# Redirects, highest precedence first.
#
# There is deliberately NO "/* /index.html 200" catch-all any more. The build
# prerenders a real HTML file for every route, so Netlify serves those files
# directly and anything genuinely unknown falls through to 404.html with a
# real 404 status. The old catch-all returned 200 for every made-up URL, which
# is a soft 404 — Google treats those as a site-quality problem — and it also
# meant the retired Wix URLs below would have served a "page not found" screen
# with a success status instead of redirecting.

# --- Wix URLs that must survive the cutover -------------------------------
# These are the URLs Google has indexed for the current Wix site (from its
# pages-sitemap.xml). Anything not carried across loses whatever ranking and
# inbound links it has accumulated. /services, /projects and /contact keep
# their slugs and need no rule; only the About page moved.

/about-us          /about      301!
/privacy-policy    /privacy    301!

# /terms-and-conditions and /accessibility-statement existed on Wix and have no
# equivalent here, so they 404 at cutover. Both were Wix's auto-generated
# boilerplate rather than anything written for this business, and a 404 is
# honest where a redirect to an unrelated page is not.
